#	Brief descn:-		Contains parmeters for cluster configuration
#******************************************************************************
# Update History
#******************************************************************************
# Ver	Date		Who		Update
#******************************************************************************
# Detailed Description
#******************************************************************************
# CLUSTER_NAME
# The name that will be updated in the cdb.cdb table on QD and all QE's.
# Note to enclose in quotes if text contains a space(s).
# MACHINE_LIST_FILE
# A file that contains a list of machine names on which the cluster will be
# installed.
#
# SEG_PREFIX
# The directory prefix where the segment database will be created, each segment
# name will be created as $DATA_DIRECTORY/$SEG_PREFIX[Seg#] where Seg# will
# start at 0 for the QD directory and increase sequentially for each QE
# directory.
#
# PORT_BASE
# The starting point for the port numbers. QD port will be $PORT_BASE, each
# QE will start at $PORT_BASE+1 for each QE on a host, so for 3 QE's per host,
# these will have ports 60001, 60002 and 60003 in this example.
#
# DATA_DIRECTORY
# The top level directory where each QE database directory will be created.
# So, for the first host with 3 QE's per host will have the following database
# directories /dbfast1/dwh1, /dbfast2/dwh2 and /dbfast3/dwh3.
# NOTE, the number in DATA_DIRECTORY determines the number of primary QE's
# per host.
#
# QD_HOSTNAME
# The hostname of the assigned QD for this cluster.
#
# QD_DATA_DIRECTORY
# The top level directory where the QD database will be created, in this example
# file the QD database directory will be /dbfast1/dwh0
#
# IP_ALLOW
# The access IP that will be placed in each QE pg_hba.conf file
#
# TRUSTED_SHELL
# The mechanism to access each QE from the QD
#
# ENV_SETUP
# The file that must be sourced on each QE to access the postgreSQL binaries.
#
# CHECK_POINT_SEGMENTS
# Number of check point segments that will be added to each QD and QE
# postgresql.conf file.
#
# ENCODING
# The encoding that will be added each QD and QE postgresql.conf file.
# 
# MIRROR_PORT_BASE
# If uncommented will set mppcreatecluster.sh to build mirror'd configuration
# using this port base for each mirror QE process.
#
# MIRROR_DATA_DIRECTORY
# If uncommented will set mppcreatecluster.sh to build mirror'd configuration
# using this top level directory for the mirror database directories
#
# STANDBY_HOST & STANDBY_IP_ALLOW
# Not configured at this release. 
#******************************************************************************
# Cluster Configuration Parameters 
#******************************************************************************
CLUSTER_NAME="DWh  Cluster"
MACHINE_LIST_FILE=`pwd`/examplempphostlist
SEG_PREFIX=dwh
PORT_BASE=60000
declare -a DATA_DIRECTORY=(/dbfast1 /dbfast2 /dbfast3)
DATABASE_PREFIX=zdwh
QD_HOSTNAME=falcon1
QD_DATA_DIRECTORY=/dbfast1
IP_ALLOW="172.16.1.0/24"
TRUSTED_SHELL="ssh"
ENV_SETUP="/usr/local/mpp/cdb-pgsql/cdb.rc"
CHECK_POINT_SEGMENTS=8
ENCODING=UNICODE

#Mirror parameters, comment out if mirroring not required
##MIRROR_PORT_BASE=45000
##declare -a MIRROR_DATA_DIRECTORY=(/dbfast3)

#Standby host parameters, comment out if not required
###STANDBY_HOST=falcon6
####STANDBY_IP_ALLOW="172.16.1.14"
